## Known caveat (does NOT block F4)

Public RPC lag-skips: gap_jumps=1178, total_slots_skipped=3721, max_single_gap=67, 0 errors /
0 rate-limits. getBlock costs ~0.7–1.2 s/slot single-threaded against a ~0.4 s/slot chain, so
`--block-max-lag 20` jumps forward routinely. Effective coverage ≈ 13–40% of slots in the sampled
window, so swaps inside skipped ranges are not observed. This is an infrastructure ceiling, not a
correctness defect: every swap that WAS observed was emitted correctly and verified on-chain.
Upgrade path: paid low-latency RPC (or multi-provider fan-out) to raise slot coverage.

